-- title:
--   Freeness of a corner of H¹(Γ_H(L),𝒪) over 𝒪[Δ]
-- statement:
--   Let $L\ge 1$, let $S$ be a set of natural numbers, let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete (adically complete for its maximal ideal) discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero whose residue field $k$ has characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, and let $H\le H'\le(\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$ with relative index $[H':H]$ a power of $p$. Assume $r\mid L$ with $r\ge 4$ and every $u\in H'$ reduces to $1$ in $\mathbb{Z}/r$. Let $\varphi\colon G\to$ [`CohCarrier.Gen L S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) assign to each index one of the formal symbols $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$), $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid L$) or $\langle d\rangle$ ($d\in(\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$), and let $dG\colon H'\to G$ satisfy $\varphi(dG\,u)=\langle u\rangle$. The operators `opFamily` realise these symbols as $\mathcal{O}$-endomorphisms of $H^1(M,H,\mathcal{O})=\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(M)^{\mathrm{ab}},\mathcal{O})$ ($T_\ell,U_q$ by the transfer-and-conjugation construction, $\langle d\rangle$ by a diamond operator); assume the images of $\varphi$ commute pairwise both at level $H$ and at level $H'$. Let $\theta bar\colon G\to k$. For the Hecke data with generators $G$, operators `opFamily` at level $H$ and system of eigenvalues $\theta bar$, let $\mathrm{Sp}$ be an idempotent splitting of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1(L,H,\mathcal{O}))$ generated by these operators (data $n$, complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$, maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal spectrum with $e_i\in\mathfrak{m}_j\iff i\ne j$), let $i_0$ be an index and $\pi k\colon \mathrm{Sp}.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0\to k$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map carrying the corner image of each operator $\mathrm{op}\,g$ to $\theta bar\,g$; let $\mathrm{Sp}',i_0',\pi k'$ be the corresponding data at level $H'$. Assume the non-Eisenstein condition: some $g$ has $\varphi(g)=T_\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 1\pmod L$ and $\theta bar\,g\ne \ell+1$. Finally let $\Delta$ be a commutative group with a homomorphism $\pi\colon(\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times\to\Delta$ whose restriction to $H'$ is onto $\Delta$ and has kernel exactly $H\cap H'=H$ inside $H'$, and let $\iota\colon \mathcal{O}[\Delta]\to \mathrm{Sp}.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map sending $\pi(u)$, $u\in H'$, to the corner image of the diamond operator $\langle u\rangle$ at level $H$. Then, with $d$ the $\mathcal{O}$-rank of the corner submodule $e_{i_0'}\cdot H^1(L,H',\mathcal{O})$, there exists a family $b\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,d\to e_{i_0}\cdot H^1(L,H,\mathcal{O})$ such that every element of $e_{i_0}\cdot H^1(L,H,\mathcal{O})$ is of the form $\sum_i \iota(c_i)\cdot b_i$ with $c_i\in\mathcal{O}[\Delta]$, and $\sum_i \iota(c_i)\cdot b_i=0$ holds if and only if all $c_i=0$; that is, the corner at level $H$ is free of rank $d$ over $\mathcal{O}[\Delta]$ acting through $\iota$.
--
--   This is the freeness assertion of the Taylor–Wiles argument (Darmon–Diamond–Taylor, Theorem 4.16(b)) in its auxiliary-level form: the localisation of $H^1$ of the smaller congruence subgroup at a non-Eisenstein maximal ideal is free over the group ring of the diamond quotient $\Delta\cong H'/H$, of rank equal to the $\mathcal{O}$-rank of the corresponding localisation at the larger level. It is used in the construction of the Taylor–Wiles level data, being cited by [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_monoidAlgebra_and_basis_ML_HQ`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_algHom_monoidAlgebra_and_basis_ML_HQ).
